# NestedText v3 — xhtml-lat1.ent sample (measured head 40/196)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/xhtml/dtd/xhtml-lat1.ent (ISO 8879 carve-out, W3C redistribution)

invocation:
    > <!ENTITY % HTMLlat1 PUBLIC "-//W3C//ENTITIES Latin 1 for XHTML//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml-lat1.ent"> then %HTMLlat1; — same declare-then-invoke as strict driver lines 26-39.

sample-rows:
    - nbsp: &#160; no-break space U+00A0 ISOnum
    - iexcl: &#161; inverted exclamation U+00A1
    - cent: &#162; pound &#163; curren &#164; yen &#165;
    - sect: &#167; uml &#168; copy &#169; reg &#174;
    - deg: &#176; plusmn &#177; sup2 &#178;

pattern-note:
    > Internal general entities mapping mnemonic -> numeric char ref + Unicode name + ISO set tag (ISOnum/ISOdia). Flat catalogue, no nesting — the precedent for our sigil collision table: $form -> meaning -> safe-form -> language-owner.
    > Remaining 156 lines same shape; strict-vs-transitional driver diff still queued.
